{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Why should we be deprived, etc.</b> One needs to know the claim of those men in saying ״לָמָּה נִגָּרַע״ — after all, the reason was on their lips, they would answer ״we are impure,״ so what did they seek, that a new Torah should be given to them? But perhaps it is because since they became impure with His permission, may He be blessed — whether according to the one who says they were impure on account of a corpse (a mitzvah) or according to the one who says they were carriers of Joseph's ark — they thought that HaShem would deal with them like the pure, and just as we find (Pesachim 77b) that HaShem is willing to allow the Paschal offering to be brought in impurity when it is a communal matter, therefore they claimed <b>why should we be deprived</b> — is it possible that because they performed a mitzvah they should be deprived of the Paschal offering? Or it may intend to say that they should make up the Paschal offering like the festal offering (חֲגִיגָה), which has make-up days throughout the seven [days of the festival], as they said (Chagigah 9a): one may keep celebrating throughout the entire festival — likewise HaShem would command them to offer the Paschal offering the next day, and this is the meaning of <b>in its appointed season</b>, which is the season of Passover." "<b>Or perhaps</b> it is for this reason that Scripture was precise in saying <b>on that day</b> — meaning, according to the one who says it was the seventh day of their impurity, therefore they came on that day so that He would tell them to make it up the next day." "<b>And according to this approach</b> we gain the reason that HaShem gave this mitzvah of the second Passover after those men had asked — to say that even if they would be pure during the days of Passover, in the case before us, even so it has no make-up to be performed during the seven days of Passover like the festal offering, but rather in the second month." "Further, it may intend the saying of <b>why should we be deprived</b> — meaning: since it was the seventh day of their impurity, they claim that they are able to slaughter their Paschal offerings on their behalf in the manner that one slaughters and sprinkles [the blood] on behalf of one impure through a creeping thing, since they become pure by evening and their impurity exists only during that day — and this is the meaning of <b>on that day</b>. And our Sages of blessed memory said other matters, and these and those are the words of the living Elohim."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:07:02.943407Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}